Still 1.2.0. Ducking: Android gets it, iPhone loses it.

On iPhone, lowering music while somebody talks means changing the audio session mid-call, and on a Bluetooth headset that stopped your background audio for good — build 184's fault. There is no way to do it without that, so the iPhone no longer lowers anything: music plays at full volume, and voices are normalised to carry over it.

On Android it works as described: quieter while somebody talks, back up fifteen seconds after.
